<section class="wrap block plans" aria-labelledby="plans-h">
  <h2 id="plans-h">Which Cloudflare plan</h2>
  <p class="section-lede">The free plan. For one person, it's plenty.</p>
  <div class="plan-row">
    <div class="card">
      <p class="plan-who">For you</p>
      <h3>Workers Free</h3>
      <p class="plan-price">$0</p>
      <p>Every machine and agent you run, on one bus.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="plan-more">
      <h3>When you'd need to upgrade</h3>
      <p>One person never gets close. You'd need Paid only if your agents send more than about 1 million messages in a day; then it's $5 a month.</p>
      <p>Workers Free includes 100,000 Durable Object requests a day, and Cloudflare counts incoming WebSocket messages 20 to 1. Past the limit, requests fail until it resets at 00:00 UTC. Nothing is billed.</p>
      <p>On Workers Paid, $5 a month includes 1 million requests, then $0.15 per million. Even a million messages a day adds only about $0.30 a month.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
